- MBD4 frameshift → Essentiality Score: 0.72 (high)
- TP53 R175H → Essentiality Score: 0.55 (moderate)
- Sequence disruption delta: 0.00012034 (significant)
Step 2: Pathway Disruption Mapping

text
MBD4 broken → BER pathway: NON_FUNCTIONAL
TP53 broken → CHECKPOINT pathway: NON_FUNCTIONAL
Result: TWO broken DNA repair systems
Step 3: Synthetic Lethality Detection

text
Broken pathways: BER + CHECKPOINT
Essential backup pathways identified: PARP, HR (homologous recombination)
Synthetic lethality detected: TRUE
Essential pathways: 4 (multi-hit vulnerability)
Add a PARP inhibitor:

text
PARP blocked → SSBs (single-strand breaks) accumulate
SSBs → Convert to DSBs (double-strand breaks) during replication
Cancer cell tries to repair DSBs → Needs BRCA/HR pathway
But: MBD4 loss creates "BRCAness" (HR deficiency)
TP53 broken → Can't trigger apoptosis (emergency exit blocked)
Result: Three broken repair systems → Catastrophic DNA damage → Cell death
Normal cells:

text
PARP blocked → SSBs accumulate
But: MBD4 intact, TP53 intact, BRCA intact
Result: Cells survive (some toxicity, but manageable)
This is synthetic lethality: The cancer dies, normal cells survive.

